/**
 * \defgroup app Application
 * \brief Entry point, state machine and shared foundations.
 *
 * This is where everything comes together: \ref mfly::AppController owns the
 * invisible control window, receives all events as posted messages and decides
 * when a flyout opens and closes again.
 */

/**
 * \defgroup detect Detection
 * \brief Determining whether the mouse pointer is over a minimize button.
 *
 * Consists of two parts: \ref mfly::HookThread delivers the mouse events
 * without holding up the system input path, and \ref CaptionProbe.h answers via
 * \c WM_NCHITTEST the question of what lies under the pointer.
 *
 * \ref mfly::DragWatcher belongs here as the touch counterpart: a finger cannot
 * hover a minimize button, so what is noticed instead is a window entering its
 * move loop - which Windows announces, and which needs no hook in the input path
 * at all.
 */

/**
 * \defgroup ui User interface
 * \brief The two windows, the monitors they draw, and stashing into the
 *        notification area.
 *
 * \ref mfly::FlyoutWindow is a menu: it is pointed at and clicked.
 * \ref mfly::ZoneOverlay is a target: it appears underneath a window that is
 * already in motion and says where it may be let go. They share their palette
 * and drawing primitives (\ref Painting.h) and the arithmetic that turns a zone
 * into a rectangle (\ref OverlayGeometry.h), so the miniature in the one and the
 * full-screen tile in the other really are the same zone.
 */

/**
 * \defgroup config Configuration and items
 * \brief Providers, configuration file and applying the window sizes.
 *
 * The text items of the flyout come without exception from providers
 * (\ref mfly::Registry). The layouts drawn above them come from
 * \c %APPDATA%\\MinFlyout\\config.jsonc: \ref mfly::ConfigStore reads the file
 * with the built-in JSONC parser (\ref Json.h), \ref mfly::ApplyZone converts
 * a zone plus its monitor into screen coordinates.
 */
